# brd-grill (Cursor)

Turn a rough Product Backlog item into a BRD by asking exactly **one
adaptive question per turn**, then write the BRD, then offer to hand off to
`prd-grill` for the implementation checklist. Don't produce the
implementation checklist yourself — that belongs to `prd-grill`.

## Before asking anything

Check for an existing BRD convention in this repo (`doc/brd/`, `docs/BRD/`,
or similar). Follow its structure if found; otherwise use the default
template below.

## Grill loop

Ask one question per turn, covering: backlog understanding in the
requester's own words, process/flow impact (yes/no + which flow), UI impact
(yes/no + which screens/forms by name), data-dictionary impact (yes/no +
what data), explicit out-of-scope. Never batch questions. Surface
contradictions with earlier answers instead of silently overwriting.

## Confirm before writing

Summarize backlog interpretation, process/UI/data impact, and scope; get
explicit confirmation before generating the file.

## Write the BRD

Default sections: Pemahaman Product Backlog, Dampak Proses/Alur (explicit
"no change" note if none), Dampak UI (explicit "no change" note if none),
Dampak Kamus Data (explicit "no change" note if none), Yang Tidak
Termasuk, Approval checklist.

If an effort-estimate table is wanted: use a 7-step rubric (Pemahaman →
Cek Flowchart → Permintaan list proses → Workflow/Flowchart → UI (only if
UI impact) → Kamus Data (only if data impact) → Pembuatan BRD). Pick ONE
overall complexity level (Rendah/Sedang/Tinggi/Sangat Tinggi) for the whole
item and apply it to every step — critical: a bundle of 2-3 small requests
is Sedang, never Tinggi, no matter how many bullets the backlog has. Apply
a 5% buffer only for Tinggi/Sangat Tinggi, showing the subtotal + buffer
arithmetic explicitly. Recompute the total from the individual step numbers
yourself rather than trusting prose arithmetic.

Write the file directly, then tell the user the exact path.

## Hand off

Ask whether to continue into the `prd-grill` skill/rule to turn the
confirmed BRD into an implementation checklist, passing along the BRD path
and the process/UI/data answers already gathered so `prd-grill` doesn't
re-ask what's already known.
